# Project Context

Paradigm is a Windows desktop app built with Tauri v2. This worktree (`src/`)
is the frontend: React + TypeScript, built with Vite. The Rust backend lives
in a separate worktree, not visible here.

## Frontend stack
- UI components: shadcn/ui
- Styling: Tailwind CSS (core utility classes)
- Data fetching / state: TanStack Query
- The app uses multiple native Tauri windows, not a single-window SPA

## Talking to the backend

Commands (all via `invoke()` from `@tauri-apps/api/core`):

- `start_record_session()` -> `Result<String, String>`
  Returns the session name. Fails if a session is already active.

- `stop_record_session()` -> `Result<CaptureSummary, String>`
  - `CaptureSummary`: `{ session_name, action_count, excluded_count, unmapped_events, actions: CapturedActionView[] }`
  - `CapturedActionView`: `{ step_order, action_type, source_app, element_role, element_name, payload_preview (null if redacted) }`
  Does NOT compile/store — this is for review only.

- `compile_and_store_playbook(name_hint?: string)` -> `Result<StoredPlaybookInfo, String>`
  - `StoredPlaybookInfo`: `{ playbook_id, label, step_count, irreversible_count, redacted_count, label_generated }`
  Uses the last stopped session — consumes it, so this can only be called once per recording.

- `list_playbooks()` -> `Result<PlaybookSummaryView[], String>`
  - `PlaybookSummaryView`: `{ id, name, source, created_at, updated_at, step_count }`

- `replay_playbook(playbookId: string)` -> `Result<ReplayReportView, String>`
  - `ReplayReportView`: `{ run_id, playbook_id, playbook_name, status ("completed"|"failed"|"aborted"), steps_total, steps_attempted, outcomes: StepOutcomeView[] }`
  - `StepOutcomeView`: `{ step_order, action_type, selector, result, detail, is_failure }`

- `get_run_history(playbookId: string)` -> `Result<RunHistoryEntry[], String>`
  - `RunHistoryEntry`: `{ run_id, feature, status, billable, started_at, completed_at, steps: StepLogView[] }`

## AI model stack (context only — frontend never calls these directly)
- Local: Qwen2.5-0.5B (Ghost Mode labeling), Qwen3.5-0.8B-Vision (fallback)
- Cloud via Fireworks AI: Qwen3-7B-Instruct (intent/form Q&A), Qwen2-VL-7B
  (heavy vision/OCR)
Useful for building appropriate loading states — cloud calls are slower and
cost real money; local calls are near-instant and free.

## Shared components
Automation Preview is a single shared confirmation component used across
Ghost Mode, Chat Mode, and Form Memory, with feature-specific variants
(first-run, failure-state/drift-repair, vision-fallback, kill-switch-disabled).
Build it once as a reusable component — don't duplicate per feature.